Remote.pm:719-721 warns:

    Git::Native: ssh host 'codeberg.org' is not in known_hosts. Run
    `ssh-keyscan codeberg.org >> ~/.ssh/known_hosts`, or set
    GIT_NATIVE_SSH_INSECURE=1 to bypass.

The advice says `~`, but never says whose. _known_hosts_match searched
$ENV{HOME}/.ssh/known_hosts, $ENV{HOME}/.ssh/known_hosts2 and
/etc/ssh/ssh_known_hosts, and it knows all three paths at that point.

Cost of not saying so, from a real session: karr runs inside a container where
HOME=/home/karr and no ~/.ssh is mounted. The user read the warning, ran
ssh-keyscan on the host as instructed, and got the identical warning again --
because the container never sees the host file. Nothing in the message hints
that the search happened somewhere else, so the natural reading is that
ssh-keyscan failed, and the search moves to the wrong place entirely. It took
comparing host_seen from a direct call (6, the host was found perfectly well
outside the container) against the warning (0) to locate the real difference.

Not a bug: the matcher is correct. It handles plain, hashed (|1| HMAC-SHA1),
[host]:port and wildcard fields, and it found the host on the host system
including entries grep cannot see. This is purely about the message.

Suggestion, in the else branch:

  - name the files that were searched, not `~`;
  - when none of the three exists or is readable, say that outright -- inside a
    container that single sentence is the whole answer.

The host_seen>0 branch above it has the same issue in milder form: it says
"the N known_hosts entries for it" without saying which file they are in.
Fixed in working tree (not committed): _known_hosts_match returns a third value %where (candidates/searched/seen_in/target); _known_hosts_warning builds the three messages from it and is the network-free test surface. HOME unset -> target undef, advice says 'set HOME'. (matched, host_seen) prefix unchanged, so t/64 is untouched and green. t/43 +5 subtests incl. a tilde-path regression assert; falsifiability verified by mutating the advice back. Changes + CLAUDE.md ('Diagnostics: never say ~') updated. Full suite: 49 files, 528 tests, PASS; t/40+t/41 skip (no live-network env vars).
